{"name":"Rhinestone","hex":"#8e6c94","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rhinestone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A diamond simulant, strass."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of or encrusted with rhinestones."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhinestone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rhinestone","blocks":[{"text":"A rhinestone, paste or diamanté is a diamond simulant originally made from rock crystal but since the 19th century from crystal glass or polymers such as acrylic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Florentiner_Glaskopie_NHM_Ay762.jpg/330px-Florentiner_Glaskopie_NHM_Ay762.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhinestone","wikidata":"Q615476"},{"title":"Rhinestone (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Rhinestone is a 1984 American musical romantic comedy film directed by Bob Clark from a screenplay by Sylvester Stallone and Phil Alden Robinson and starring Stallone, Dolly Parton, Richard Farnsworth and Ron Leibman. It is based on the 1975 hit song \"Rhinestone Cowboy\" written by Larry Weiss. Although a critical and financial failure, the film spawned two top 10 country hits for Parton on the Billboard Hot Country Songs chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9d/Rhinestone_%28movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhinestone_(film)","wikidata":"Q1071169"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Strass.jpg/500px-Strass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Strass.jpg/500px-Strass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rhinestones on a tiara","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStrass.jpg"},{"srcset":"